    "title": "Iowa State Fair slightly behind 2024's attendance record - NewsBreak",
    "text": "DES MOINES , Iowa ( KCAU ) — Halfway through this year’s Iowa State Fair, attendance numbers are slightly behind 2024’s record attendance. More than 1,182,000 people went through the gates last year. After the first six days of this year’s state fair, just more than 630,000 fans have been on the ground. Story continues below That’s around 12,000 fewer at the same point last summer. Again, 2024 was a record year for attendance. Nearly sold-out grandstand concerts from Hank Williams Jr. and Def Leppard are expected to help push attendance numbers, with three of the fair’s most attended days still to come. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to SiouxlandProud | Sioux City, IA | News, Weather, and Sports.",
